-- NEGATIVE fixture, and the file that KEEPS A CONCESSION HONEST (spec §6.4.5,
-- and §2.4.1's L12).
--
-- p4, second variant: the WHERE-local recurses ON ITSELF, and no top-level name
-- participates.
--
--     `the settled value` MEANS `fixpoint`
--                         WHERE `fixpoint` MEANS `fixpoint`
--
-- §6.4.5 concedes that this is INVISIBLE to any graph whose nodes are
-- decisions: the only cycle is inside one node, so no SCC over the DRG can
-- report it however correct the SCC is. Today it is caught incidentally, by
-- D-LITERALEXPR, because the body does not render -- which is luck, not a
-- check.
--
-- The fixture exists so that the concession has a witness. If a future change
-- makes the body render, D-LITERALEXPR stops firing, and this file becomes a
-- SILENT non-terminating decision unless something else is added. That is a
-- regression the concession predicted and this file is how it gets noticed.
--
-- Expected: NO D-CYCLE and NO D-RECURSIVE, deliberately, plus whatever note the
-- unrenderable body draws. If a cycle finding ever DOES appear here, the graph
-- grew nodes it did not have, and §6.4.5 needs rereading rather than the
-- fixture needing fixing.
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `self recursive where local`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the settled value` MEANS
    `fixpoint`
      WHERE
        `fixpoint` MEANS `fixpoint` PLUS 0
